      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change cannot be upstreamed because it alters the default fill-silence behavior. Instead of inserting silence, the `fill_silence` call fills the buffer with a very low-amplitude, high-frequency signal outside the audible range. On our Android product, this functionality is exposed as a UI-controlled custom feature called \"comfort noise,\" which keeps receivers active and avoids startup latency that could clip the beginning of the audio stream.",
